 TheSeed Auto-Sync Daemon Configuration * Roadmap: 02_REPO_ARCHITECTURE.md §6, §9.3 * Place this file next to auto-sync.ps1: TheSeed/scripts/auto-sync.config.json * * IMPORTANT: This config is in JSON5-style comments for documentation. * Remove all comments ( and  ) before use, or PowerShell's * ConvertFrom-Json will fail. Pure JSON only!  {  Sync interval in minutes. Default: 5  'interval_minutes': 5,  Branches to watch and sync. Must match your branching model: * main    -> Production, tagged releases * develop -> Integration, CI runs here * * Per Roadmap §3.1: main + develop + feature/mX-* * Only list branches you want auto-synced.  'branches': [ 'main', 'develop' ],  If true, stashes uncommitted changes before pull, * restores them after. Prevents data loss. * Solo-Dev Safety feature.  'stash_on_dirty': true,  If true, runs a quick cmake build check after sync * to catch broken builds immediately. * Requires build/ directory to exist.  'test_after_sync': false,  Max log file size in MB before rotation. * Old logs are renamed to auto-sync.log.YYYYMMDD-HHMMSS  'max_log_size_mb': 10,  Discord webhook URL for error notifications. * Leave null to disable. * Format: 'https:discord.com/api/webhooks/...'  'discord_webhook': null }